/*
 * Playwright-Java port of the original Selenium WebUtil class.
 *
 * Mapping notes (Selenium -> Playwright):
 *  - WebDriver              -> Page (per-thread, held by ThreadLocal exactly like poolDriver before)
 *  - WebElement             -> Locator (Playwright locators are lazily-resolved and auto-wait,
 *                              so most of the retry/exception-handling that Selenium needed is no
 *                              longer necessary - Playwright actions already wait for actionability)
 *  - JavascriptExecutor     -> page.evaluate() / locator.evaluate()
 *  - Actions class          -> Locator.hover()/dblclick()/dragTo(), Mouse (page.mouse())
 *  - Select class           -> Locator.selectOption(...)
 *  - WebDriverWait/Expected
 *    Conditions             -> Locator.waitFor(WaitForOptions) - Playwright auto-waits on every
 *                              action, so explicit waits are only needed for custom conditions
 *  - Window handles         -> BrowserContext.pages() (Playwright has no window "handles"; each
 *                              popup/tab is its own Page inside the same BrowserContext)
 *  - Frame handling         -> Page.frameLocator(selector) / Page.frames()
 *  - Alerts                 -> Page.onDialog(Dialog handler)
 *
 * Because Playwright already retries and auto-waits internally, most of the duplicated
 * "catch specific exception, retry once" blocks from the Selenium version are collapsed into a
 * single try/catch that logs failure to ExtentReports and rethrows - the retry itself is handled
 * by Playwright's own actionability checks.
 */
public class WebUtil {

